description = [=[mod id 3787803421

[b]A Shine extension that lets aliens call their lifeform before the round starts.[/b]

Open the scoreboard during the pre-round, click the lifeform icon on your own row, and pick what you intend to play. Your pick shows on the scoreboard for your team and for spectators.

[b]It has no gameplay effect at all.[/b] Nothing is reserved, gated, or forced — you still evolve exactly as normal. It only replaces "who's going fade" in voice chat with something the whole team can read at a glance.

[h1]How to use it[/h1]

[list]
[*] Join the alien team during the pre-round.
[*] Hold the scoreboard key. Every alien has a lifeform icon on their row, defaulting to Skulk.
[*] Click [b]your own[/b] icon. A "Planned Lifeform" menu opens at your cursor: Skulk, Gorge, Lerk, Fade, Onos.
[*] Pick one. Every alien and spectator sees it immediately.
[/list]

Hovering any icon names the lifeform it shows — "Planned Lifeform: Lerk" — in the same style as the scoreboard's badge and skill tooltips.

The icons only appear before a round starts, and disappear the moment it begins.

[h1]Greyed out vs. lit up[/h1]

An icon is [b]greyed out[/b] until its owner has actually confirmed it for the round about to start, and [b]cream[/b] once they have. That distinction is the point of the whole thing: it separates "this player has told us they are going Fade" from "we are only assuming, because nobody has said otherwise".

[list]
[*] Anyone who has never picked shows a grey Skulk — the assumed default, not a statement of intent.
[*] Picking a lifeform lights your icon cream immediately.
[*] [b]Your pick is remembered between rounds.[/b] It is never forgotten, but when a round starts or resets it drops back to grey, still showing the lifeform you last chose.
[*] To light it up again for the new round, click your icon and pick — including picking the same lifeform you already had. Re-picking what you already have still counts as confirming it.
[/list]

So a grey Onos means "this player went Onos last round and has not said what they are doing this time", while a cream Onos means "this player has committed to Onos for this round".

[h1]Who sees what[/h1]

[list]
[*] [b]Aliens[/b] — see all picks, can declare.
[*] [b]The alien commander[/b] — sees all picks, but has no icon of their own and cannot declare; there is nothing for them to evolve into while they are in the chair. A pick made before taking the chair is hidden rather than erased, and returns if they log out.
[*] [b]Spectators[/b] — see all picks, cannot declare.
[*] [b]Marines[/b] — see nothing. Picks are filtered on the server, so the data never reaches a marine's machine at all rather than being sent and merely hidden.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]

[list]
[*] Requires [b]Shine[/b]. It installs as a normal Shine extension and is enabled by default; toggle it with [i]sh_loadplugin lifeformpicker[/i].
[*] Must be run on the server.
[/list]

[h1]Credits[/h1]

The idea, and the click-your-icon-for-a-menu interaction, come from Hatta's discontinued [i]Shine - Lifeform Selector[/i], used with his permission.

The lifeform artwork .dds file with the vanilla icons comes from [i]Shimizu Scoreboard[/i], used with his permission.

This is an independent implementation rather than a fork of any of them.

Source: https://github.com/Bleuitup/Shine-Lifeform-Picker]=]
